      "value": "# ref_video: S22-c03_ref.mp4\n\nsubject_definitions:\n\n<Subject 1> is the person shown in <Video 1>, as in the reference video, shown in <Picture 1>. She is the one in <Video 1>.\n\n\n\nsummary:\n\n[video editing + audio reuse] A single continuous 2D-animated rotoscope scene of the person shown in <Video 1> in <Video 1>, preserving appearance from the reference pictures and the timing, posture, and speech of the reference video.\n\n\n\nretention_analysis:\n\n<Subject 1>: fully_preserved \u2014 keep as in the reference video consistent across [Shot 1], [Shot 2], [Shot 3] and <Video 1>.\n<Video 1>: attribute_transfer \u2014 carry the posture, facial performance, and exact spoken dialogue and delivery into the clip.\nDialogue audio of <Video 1>: fully_copy \u2014 reuse the spoken lines and timing.\n\n\n\ndetailed_description:\n\n2D-animated rotoscope painted animation in the style of a 1983 fantasy film: inked figures over cool-toned painted stone interiors, cold blue-grey cavern light\n\n[Shot 1] The camera stays low and tilts up slightly as the figure moves. The camera pushes in with small amplitude at slow speed, tightening toward the face. the person shown in <Video 1>.\n\n[Shot 2] At 00:03.295, The camera pushes in with small amplitude at slow speed, tightening toward the face.\n\n[Shot 3] At 00:05.088, The camera pulls out with small amplitude at slow speed, opening the space around the figures. The move slows and stops as the figure settles.\n\n\n\noverall_soundscape:\n\nRoom tone and air movement throughout, cloth rustle with every body movement, footsteps wherever anyone moves.\n\n\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\n\nLow sustained strings and slow woodwind pulses at a slow tempo, with sparse bell tones above; dynamics stay quiet and grow only slightly."
